      "architectural_implications": [
        "1. No Canonical/Smt contamination in statement files: All 8 sampled statement-only .lean files in proofnet-verified/ (tree 394620c77ebfc275c4cd4e740a2d7c0926b2d8a5) only `import Mathlib` and end in `:= by sorry`; none import `Canonical` or `Smt` (which only appear in upstream lakefile.lean).",
        "2. Header structure (`open` / `open scoped` + `import Mathlib`): Upstream ProofNet-Verified files use `import Mathlib` plus `open` / `open scoped` header lines (e.g. `open Filter Real Topology`, `open scoped Topology BigOperators`), whereas `lean_worker.py` currently admits a fixed module allowlist (`ALLOWED_IMPORTS`) and renders `import <mod>` directly before `theorem irisx_final <declaration> :=`. Supporting arbitrary upstream textbook statements in a future revision would require either per-item submodule imports + scoped namespace bindings inside the declaration or an explicitly reviewed header field in `statement_digest`.",
        "3. Runtime & cache boundary: Upstream ProofNet-Verified targets Lean v4.28.0 + full `import Mathlib` (`8f9d9cff6bd728b17a24e163c9402775d9e6a365`), whereas our frozen local WSL Mathlib project (`d0bb542569dd4742f2b883fea29caf41be39694a3d776c47a5a70d013c8faf79`) is pinned to Lean v4.19.0 (`c44e0c8ee63ca166450922a373c7409c5d26b00b`) with the 691-file `Ring`/`NormNum` cache closure.",
        "4. Denominator boundary: All 367 files in `proofnet-verified/` are pure `prove` tasks (the 4 non-proof items were removed upstream), so ProofNet-Verified alone cannot supply the `find_answer` denominator required for the joint answer+proof hypothesis.",
        "5. Sequencing rule per independent review 5568170709: Do not modify tracked runtime files (`lean_worker.py`, `controller.py`, `protocol.json`, `panel-proposal.json`) before Kaggle TPU smoke reconciliation and M2-SMOKE qualification."
      ]
